WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:04.780
Fight, crash through, and face the challenge!

3
00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:08.000
These are our hard knock days.

4
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.830
Can't quench our thirst with a peaceful, everyday life.

5
00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:15.340
Here we go - don't ever run away!

6
00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:19.450
Let's go on living as the mighty winds take us!

7
00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:21.870
We've still got so far to go.

8
00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:26.390
Gotta keep going through the hard knock days.

9
00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:31.610
Let's do it again, yes, baby. How many times

10
00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:34.110
do I have to stand back up to make my dream come true?

11
00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:36.730
Feels like the strength of my resolve

12
00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:39.200
is put to the test everyday.

13
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:40.700
Hey, let's go!

14
00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:44.450
I don't want to make excuses and settle for being mediocre.

15
00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:45.900
Hey, let's go!

16
00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:49.670
We leapt into a crazy, lawless world.

17
00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:54.110
As I struggled for a foothold, reality caught me off guard.

18
00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:59.370
Even if it beats me, hits me, knocks me down again,

19
00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:00.220
Oh!

20
00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:04.500
Only when we get back on our feet and look forward,

21
00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:07.450
will we have the last laugh, be the winners!

22
00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:10.120
We gotta go down this glory road, till we reach our goal!

23
00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:12.630
Fight, shake it off, act strong!

24
00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:15.630
These are our hard knock days.

25
00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:20.680
There's no such thing as a safe choice.

26
00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.890
Here we go - we'll always be the strongest!

27
00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:27.270
Let's keep moving - never mind the consequences.

28
00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:29.860
Let's put our wishes all together,

29
00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:34.650
and keep on going through the hard knock days.

30
00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:45.780
<b>Sabo's Adventure</b>

31
00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:50.270
<b>Dressrosa
A Hill in the Eastern Town of Carta</b>

32
00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:57.820
<b>Kyros' House</b>

33
00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:04.250
So you met him while with the Revolutionary Army?

34
00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:04.860
Yes.

35
00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:06.170
Luffy...

36
00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:08.700
Robin, you don't have to wake him.

37
00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:11.920
I just came to see his face before I set off.

38
00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:17.790
Are you leaving the country already?

39
00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:21.750
Yeah. Trouble's headed this way.

40
00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:23.080
What kind of trouble?

41
00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:24.260
CP-0.

42
00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:31.820
They played a part in Doflamingo's deception scheme.

43
00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:52.800
And they're targeting us.

44
00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:01.560
Dressrosa's gonna get busy in a day or two.

45
00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:04.360
You guys should also leave as soon as possible.

46
00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:07.140
Thank you for telling us.

47
00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:11.680
And what's more, I didn't know he had another brother besides Ace.

48
00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:14.370
For real, this is the first I've heard of it.

49
00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:15.480
I bet.

50
00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:18.760
I think it surprised Luffy the most.

51
00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:22.500
What do you mean by that?

52
00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:26.060
I was presumed dead for a long time.

53
00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:32.900
I was always with Luffy and Ace when I was a kid.

54
00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:38.780
Running around with wild abandon,
being disciplined by that old man, Garp,

55
00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:41.080
dreaming about becoming pirates...

56
00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:59.300
And we exchanged cups of sake and became brothers.

57
00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:08.100
But one day, I was involved in an accident.

58
00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.470
Uh, well, an incident.

59
00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:14.520
Ace! Luffy!

60
00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:17.600
There's something wrong with this town! They're all mad!

61
00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:23.630
They all know people are going to die, but they're acting like nothing's wrong. They're even smiling!

62
00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:25.810
I don't want to be in this town!

63
00:04:25.810 --> 00:04:27.660
I have to tell them as soon as possible!

64
00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:33.740
Ace! Luffy! Run!

65
00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:44.840
What happened to you, young boy?

66
00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:57.030
This town smells worse than the Gray Terminal!

67
00:04:57.640 --> 00:05:01.410
It's the disgusting stench of rotten people!

68
00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:08.160
I'll never be free if I stay here!

69
00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:20.160
Ace... Luffy...

70
00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:24.220
I really want to see you...

71
00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:27.880
This place is like a bird cage...

72
00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:34.520
I'm not sure if I can bear living in
this kingdom, breathing this stale air.

73
00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:42.900
Just what... is freedom?

74
00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:45.520
Where can I find it?

75
00:05:57.940 --> 00:06:00.600
Ace... Luffy...

76
00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:05.210
Somebody... help me...

77
00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:06.320
Help...

78
00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:27.760
Vyou're late, Dragon!

79
00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:30.260
How long did vyou plan to keep vus waiting?!

80
00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:31.240
Sorry.

81
00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:33.440
Vyou... What's that?

82
00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:38.230
Th-This is awful!

83
00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:41.310
You! Quickly, bring a doctor! This is an emergency!

84
00:06:41.310 --> 00:06:43.030
Call the ship's doctor, quickly!

85
00:06:47.820 --> 00:06:49.180
He's awake!

86
00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:52.310
Please don't shock him.

87
00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:54.750
Vi wasn't trying to do that!

88
00:06:54.750 --> 00:06:56.600
Oh, vyou're so rude!

89
00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:01.810
Huh?

90
00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:04.880
Where am I?

91
00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:06.750
You're on board our ship.

92
00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:14.410
It says "Sabo" on your possessions. Is that your name?

93
00:07:14.980 --> 00:07:16.130
Sabo?

94
00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:18.610
Dunno.

95
00:07:18.610 --> 00:07:22.400
"Dunno"? So what is vyour name, then?

96
00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:26.120
No idea...

97
00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:28.050
Don't tell me he's...

98
00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:29.060
Most likely.

99
00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:34.800
He still hasn't regained his memories?

100
00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:37.290
Indeed, not even his own name.

101
00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:42.790
I first met him in High Town, Goa Kingdom.

102
00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:46.210
I'm certain he's one of the nobles from there.

103
00:07:46.210 --> 00:07:49.720
Well, let's take him home then. Search for his parents...

104
00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:53.670
No...

105
00:07:53.670 --> 00:07:55.270
I don't wanna go back!

106
00:07:55.270 --> 00:07:56.820
Why?

107
00:07:56.820 --> 00:07:58.090
I dunno!

108
00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:00.710
But...

109
00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:04.250
that's the last thing I want!

110
00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:08.340
So you've had amnesia up until two years ago?

111
00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:09.220
Yeah.

112
00:08:09.220 --> 00:08:12.880
If it was that serious,
just how did you get your memory back?

113
00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:15.580
Ace helped me.

114
00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:19.540
That's what I think, anyway.

115
00:08:19.420 --> 00:08:20.370
Fire Fist Ace Dies

116
00:08:22.380 --> 00:08:24.960
The timing couldn't have been any worse, but...

117
00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.400
That was how...

118
00:08:31.990 --> 00:08:34.380
...he woke me up.

119
00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:47.100
<b>Baltigo
Revolutionary Army General Headquarters</b>

120
00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:52.690
It's so hectic.

121
00:08:52.690 --> 00:08:55.390
Oh, Chief Sabo! You came at the right time!

122
00:08:55.390 --> 00:08:57.210
Report to the situation room at once!

123
00:08:57.210 --> 00:09:01.800
The Paramount War between the Navy and the Whitebeard Pirates has ended!

124
00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:05.230
Whitebeard lost?!

125
00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:07.370
Is Iva-san alright?!

126
00:09:07.370 --> 00:09:10.010
He's not listed among the casualties.

127
00:09:10.010 --> 00:09:12.050
The dead include...

128
00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:15.390
The Emperor, Whitebeard...

129
00:09:15.390 --> 00:09:16.890
and...

130
00:09:16.890 --> 00:09:18.420
Fire Fist Ace!

131
00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:28.140
But more importantly, Dragon-san, this here...

132
00:09:28.140 --> 00:09:32.760
Is it true?
Is Straw Hat Luffy your son?

133
00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:33.700
Hmm?

134
00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:34.760
Yes.

135
00:09:59.380 --> 00:10:00.920
I'm gonna become a pirate...

136
00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:10.000
...defeat everyone in my way, and be known worldwide!

137
00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:13.650
That'll be proof enough that I once lived!

138
00:10:34.540 --> 00:10:36.100
Sabo-kun, what's wrong?

139
00:10:39.480 --> 00:10:40.480
You're acting weird!

140
00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:53.050
Have you heard?

141
00:10:54.820 --> 00:10:58.240
They say Akainu punched a hole right through his body!

142
00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:07.820
When you exchange sake cups, you become brothers.

143
00:11:08.920 --> 00:11:12.270
No matter where we are or what we do,
our bonds won't be broken!

144
00:11:15.820 --> 00:11:17.980
So from now on, we're...

145
00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:19.910
brothers!

146
00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:27.860
Yeah!

147
00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:38.120
Are you alright, Sabo?

148
00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:52.770
Sabo-kun!

149
00:11:52.770 --> 00:11:53.720
Sabo!

150
00:11:55.960 --> 00:11:57.140
That's right...

151
00:11:58.540 --> 00:12:01.820
This dead guy wasn't just some random pirate...

152
00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:11.980
He wasn't just some threat in the
Pirate Era that needed to be eliminated!

153
00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:18.330
Ace is my...

154
00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:21.180
brother!

155
00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:37.140
I won't run from, or lose to anyone!

156
00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:47.170
The Chief of Staff''s awake!

157
00:12:47.170 --> 00:12:49.440
Really? What a relief!

158
00:12:59.020 --> 00:13:02.600
I thought you were gonna die, Sabo-kun!

159
00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:06.420
You had quite a high fever, Sabo.

160
00:13:07.060 --> 00:13:09.650
You were asleep for three days straight!

161
00:13:09.650 --> 00:13:12.420
I was so worried!

162
00:13:17.740 --> 00:13:19.980
Huh? You've got your memory back?

163
00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:24.940
Yeah, I remember everything now.

164
00:13:24.940 --> 00:13:30.720
Including who I am and why I
left home and sailed out to sea.

165
00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:35.800
I see. Good for you.

166
00:13:36.980 --> 00:13:38.940
Are you gonna quit the Revolutionary Army, then?!

167
00:13:42.940 --> 00:13:44.660
Nope, no way.

168
00:13:47.460 --> 00:13:49.290
Is Dragon-san still here?

169
00:13:49.290 --> 00:13:49.920
Yeah.

170
00:13:51.480 --> 00:13:53.030
There's something I want to talk about.

171
00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:12.440
At that moment, I felt Ace say to me,

172
00:14:12.440 --> 00:14:16.380
"You're Sabo. You're brothers with me and Luffy."

173
00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:43.500
Finally... I've managed to come this far, Ace.

174
00:14:45.460 --> 00:14:46.700
Check it out.

175
00:14:46.700 --> 00:14:51.020
Luffy's started on his way again to become the Pirate King.

176
00:14:52.060 --> 00:14:54.280
That's our little brother for you!

177
00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:55.580
Headline: The Straw Hats Are Back

178
00:15:16.800 --> 00:15:17.920
Sabo-kun?

179
00:15:17.920 --> 00:15:20.310
I want you to ask a favor of
the entire Revolutionary Army.

180
00:15:21.040 --> 00:15:23.860
There's a Devil Fruit that I need to acquire, no matter the cost.

181
00:15:23.930 --> 00:15:27.500
<b>Dressrosa</b>

182
00:15:25.700 --> 00:15:27.620
But, but Luffy-senpai...

183
00:15:27.620 --> 00:15:29.420
What about the Flame Fruit?

184
00:15:29.420 --> 00:15:32.540
There's someone I really don't want to have it,
but I got no choice.

185
00:15:32.540 --> 00:15:34.550
My friends' lives are more important.

186
00:15:37.480 --> 00:15:40.970
Ah'll definitely get ya the Flame Fruit!

187
00:15:40.970 --> 00:15:43.550
Just go do whatever it was ya needed to!

188
00:15:43.550 --> 00:15:45.300
Really? Thanks a bunch!

189
00:15:51.920 --> 00:15:54.560
I won't let you have the Flame Fruit...

190
00:15:57.900 --> 00:16:00.010
Straw Hat Luffy.

191
00:16:01.400 --> 00:16:03.970
Hey, hey, hey! Who're you?

192
00:16:03.970 --> 00:16:07.320
Why're you just casually talking to Luffy-senpai like that?

193
00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:12.670
He's the younger brother of that legendary pirate, Fire Fist Ace-sama,

194
00:16:12.670 --> 00:16:16.770
and the future Pirate King, you dumbass!

195
00:16:16.770 --> 00:16:19.000
I've known that for a long time.

196
00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:29.510
What's your problem?!

197
00:16:29.510 --> 00:16:32.730
Just showing up outta nowhere and telling me
you won't let me have the Flame Fruit!

198
00:16:41.480 --> 00:16:43.440
It's me, Luffy.

199
00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:47.630
What do you mean, "It's me"?!

200
00:16:47.630 --> 00:16:50.940
Get this! The Flame Fruit is a keepsake of Ace's!

201
00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:52.200
If you want it, we're enemies!

202
00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:55.750
And as for you calling me "Luffy"...

203
00:16:55.750 --> 00:16:57.490
See this beard?

204
00:16:57.490 --> 00:16:59.120
I'm Lucy!

205
00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:03.300
You really think I wouldn't know my little brother's face behind that disguise of his?

206
00:17:03.880 --> 00:17:05.410
"Little brother"?

207
00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:08.150
Look here, the only people allowed to call me "little brother"...

208
00:17:08.150 --> 00:17:09.570
are Ace, who's dead, and...

209
00:17:09.570 --> 00:17:11.310
a guy who died way earlier...

210
00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:29.660
Sabo!

211
00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:35.500
You can't be him!

212
00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:43.400
We stole a bottle of sake from Dadan and made a toast...

213
00:17:48.980 --> 00:17:51.380
Sabo!

214
00:18:00.880 --> 00:18:04.770
What the hell?! Where have you been this whole time?!

215
00:18:04.770 --> 00:18:07.580
I thought you were dead!

216
00:18:11.680 --> 00:18:13.620
Thank you, Luffy!

217
00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:17.540
I'm glad you lived!

218
00:18:23.840 --> 00:18:26.720
But Sabo, I...

219
00:18:26.720 --> 00:18:30.100
I let Ace be killed right in front of me...

220
00:18:30.720 --> 00:18:34.740
I know. Even though Ace died, I'm...

221
00:18:35.980 --> 00:18:37.740
so happy that you survived!

222
00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:42.860
I almost lost both of my brothers without being able to do a thing!

223
00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:48.580
If you'd died too, I would've been left on my own!

224
00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:07.430
So, thanks!

225
00:19:10.140 --> 00:19:13.220
Thanks for staying alive, Luffy!

226
00:19:22.480 --> 00:19:25.840
Is it alright if I eat the Flame Fruit?

227
00:19:27.700 --> 00:19:29.000
Uh-huh!

228
00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:34.070
That'd be great! Nobody else can have it!

229
00:19:42.460 --> 00:19:45.000
That darn Luffy... He's smiling!

230
00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:48.620
Makes you wonder what he's dreaming about.

231
00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:53.390
Well, I'm off.

232
00:19:53.390 --> 00:19:54.360
So soon?

233
00:19:54.360 --> 00:19:55.950
I got to see his face, so...

234
00:19:55.950 --> 00:19:59.040
Here, I had a Vivre Card made from Luffy, just in case.

235
00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:02.220
Oh? When'd you have time for that?

236
00:20:02.220 --> 00:20:03.650
I'll be taking a piece.

237
00:20:06.200 --> 00:20:09.350
Alright. Luffy may be a bit of a handful,

238
00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:10.740
but please take good care of him.

239
00:20:13.420 --> 00:20:15.440
Yeah! You can count on us!

240
00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:22.180
He and Ace said the same thing.

241
00:20:28.500 --> 00:20:30.710
Sabo, that you? Hack here.

242
00:20:30.710 --> 00:20:33.740
Yeah, I just left. I'll be back soon.

243
00:20:33.740 --> 00:20:35.020
Roger that.

244
00:20:35.020 --> 00:20:38.280
So, how'd it go? Luffy-kun was quite...

245
00:20:43.440 --> 00:20:44.670
Why'd he hang up?!

246
00:20:44.670 --> 00:20:45.660
That selfish jerk!

247
00:20:46.440 --> 00:20:47.820
Whoa there, Hack-san!

248
00:21:02.640 --> 00:21:04.370
We're all set to depart, right?

249
00:21:04.370 --> 00:21:06.270
Yeah, anytime.

250
00:21:06.270 --> 00:21:07.380
Alright!

251
00:21:07.380 --> 00:21:11.600
Once we return to Baltigo, there's so much I have to tell Dragon-san about Luffy!

252
00:21:13.560 --> 00:21:15.160
I really am...

253
00:21:15.160 --> 00:21:17.220
glad I got to see him again.

254
00:21:18.740 --> 00:21:19.620
Let's move out!

255
00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:29.900
<b>Dressrosa</b>

256
00:21:33.420 --> 00:21:37.540
What is it? Could you look for me?

257
00:21:37.540 --> 00:21:38.480
It's a "one".

258
00:21:39.080 --> 00:21:43.610
I see. The only side that would be in Straw Hat's favor...

259
00:21:43.610 --> 00:21:45.460
That's what we agreed upon, yes?

260
00:21:45.460 --> 00:21:47.120
Yes, it is, but...

261
00:21:47.120 --> 00:21:50.620
Then, he won this one.

262
00:21:51.980 --> 00:21:54.190
We shan't arrest him tonight.

263
00:21:54.190 --> 00:21:56.960
You can't determine that just by a roll of the die, Isshou-san!

264
00:21:56.960 --> 00:22:01.190
We ran all over the entire country and finally found out where he is!

265
00:22:01.190 --> 00:22:04.270
After all the disrespect you showed Fleet Admiral Sakazuki...

266
00:22:04.270 --> 00:22:07.630
If we want to take down Law and Straw Hat, now's our chance!

267
00:22:07.630 --> 00:22:09.180
Maynard-san!

268
00:22:09.960 --> 00:22:15.180
A man ought not complain after the die is cast.

269
00:22:15.740 --> 00:22:18.320
Quite pathetic of you, really.

270
00:22:20.310 --> 00:22:23.230
<b>Royal Palace</b>

271
00:22:23.520 --> 00:22:26.660
Has anyone seen Lucy after all that?

272
00:22:26.660 --> 00:22:28.010
No, nobody did.

273
00:22:28.010 --> 00:22:29.560
I just wanna thank him!

274
00:22:29.560 --> 00:22:31.710
There's already quite a fuss out there.

275
00:22:31.710 --> 00:22:34.690
Even if they truly are pirates or criminals,

276
00:22:34.690 --> 00:22:38.220
they're unquestionably our saviors.

277
00:22:44.760 --> 00:22:45.760
Grandfather!

278
00:22:47.180 --> 00:22:48.600
Rebecca.

279
00:22:48.600 --> 00:22:52.080
Father, Lucy, and the others aren't here at the Palace!

280
00:22:52.080 --> 00:22:57.300
Ah, don't worry about that. Kyros called.

281
00:22:57.300 --> 00:22:59.180
They're all together.

282
00:23:00.320 --> 00:23:00.960
I see.

283
00:23:03.160 --> 00:23:04.460
That aside...

284
00:23:05.380 --> 00:23:06.560
Rebecca.

285
00:23:09.320 --> 00:23:12.240
If I were to return as king,

286
00:23:12.880 --> 00:23:15.560
that would make you a princess.

287
00:23:17.940 --> 00:23:23.000
<b>The Next Day
The New World
(The Twirly Hat Pirates)</b>

288
00:23:31.420 --> 00:23:33.140
Damn!

289
00:23:33.720 --> 00:23:37.560
We finally shook off Big Mom's ship
after all that trouble...

290
00:23:39.920 --> 00:23:42.540
So why would you get us into even more trouble?!

291
00:23:43.440 --> 00:23:45.960
You've no say in the matter!

292
00:23:45.960 --> 00:23:46.750
Do as you're told!

293
00:23:46.750 --> 00:23:49.140
I'm saying it for the sake of you guys!

294
00:23:49.900 --> 00:23:52.700
Don't stick your nose in their business!

295
00:23:52.700 --> 00:23:57.690
We should have waited patiently on the ship.
You're pretty stupid to be rushing ahead like this!

296
00:23:57.690 --> 00:24:00.150
Shut up and do what I tell you!

297
00:24:00.150 --> 00:24:01.160
You gonna do it?!

298
00:24:01.940 --> 00:24:04.560
Or would you rather I crush your heart?!

299
00:24:10.200 --> 00:24:12.790
Fine! But I won't forget this.

300
00:24:14.280 --> 00:24:16.650
It was the right call to come ashore!

301
00:24:16.650 --> 00:24:21.340
We can still save them! We need your help!

302
00:24:22.380 --> 00:24:25.790
In that case, why don't you treat me more nicely...

303
00:24:25.790 --> 00:24:26.940
You say something?!

304
00:24:27.920 --> 00:24:30.280
Stop threatening me with that!

305
00:24:30.280 --> 00:24:31.850
Hurry up, Caesar!

306
00:24:31.850 --> 00:24:35.340
Stop telling me what to do, you blasted raccoon dog!

307
00:24:36.040 --> 00:24:38.080
I'm a reindeer!

308
00:24:38.080 --> 00:24:40.300
What's the difference?!

309
00:24:40.300 --> 00:24:43.580
Shut up! Just hurry up!

310
00:24:46.060 --> 00:24:50.420
If they die because of you, I'll make you pay for it!

311
00:24:51.460 --> 00:24:54.680
We need your help!

312
00:25:05.200 --> 00:25:07.480
It's hard to run here!

313
00:25:07.480 --> 00:25:10.900
I can't believe we were separated
from Sanji-san and the others.

314
00:25:10.900 --> 00:25:11.980
We're in trouble!

315
00:25:12.540 --> 00:25:15.260
We were too captivated by the mystery girl.

316
00:25:17.540 --> 00:25:20.340
Oh, watch out, Nami-san!

317
00:25:21.900 --> 00:25:23.920
Watch out, me!

318
00:25:25.920 --> 00:25:28.160
No, how could you?!
How could you?! How could you?!

319
00:25:32.220 --> 00:25:34.020
Onami, they are upon us!

320
00:25:39.520 --> 00:25:41.200
Yahoo!

321
00:25:56.020 --> 00:25:59.250
Is this it, invaders?

322
00:25:59.250 --> 00:26:02.360
Hey! Where'd you hide that girl?

323
00:26:03.380 --> 00:26:06.080
How'd you guys make it onto this island?

324
00:26:06.940 --> 00:26:10.070
Answer me! This place is pretty hard to-

325
00:26:10.860 --> 00:26:13.200
What... what's going on?!

326
00:26:13.200 --> 00:26:14.800
What is it this time?!

327
00:26:19.540 --> 00:26:21.960
It's a Rain-Ruption!

328
00:26:22.880 --> 00:26:23.680
Again?

329
00:26:24.760 --> 00:26:26.540
Get down!

330
00:26:29.400 --> 00:26:31.230
What is that?!

331
00:26:31.230 --> 00:26:32.560
"Rain"?

332
00:26:32.560 --> 00:26:34.840
That's way off! It's a deluge!

333
00:26:36.980 --> 00:26:40.060
I shall protect you no matter what!

334
00:26:47.380 --> 00:26:49.620
No!

335
00:26:50.280 --> 00:26:51.640
Nami-san!

336
00:26:52.380 --> 00:26:54.340
Momonosuke-san!

337
00:26:55.120 --> 00:26:58.540
Help me!

338
00:26:59.320 --> 00:27:01.050
Assist me, too!

339
00:27:01.050 --> 00:27:01.910
Geez!

340
00:27:01.910 --> 00:27:04.420
You Devil Fruit users are such pains in the butt!

341
00:27:04.420 --> 00:27:08.080
I'm sorry I couldn't protect you!

342
00:27:11.240 --> 00:27:15.360
You won't get away from me, you damned invaders!

343
00:27:28.640 --> 00:27:30.640
Come on, pull yourself together!

344
00:27:31.600 --> 00:27:33.670
Thank you, as always.

345
00:27:33.670 --> 00:27:35.390
You too, Momo!

346
00:27:35.390 --> 00:27:36.740
I am in your debt.

347
00:27:40.960 --> 00:27:43.080
When in doubt...

348
00:27:43.080 --> 00:27:44.400
Just kill!

349
00:27:50.160 --> 00:27:51.090
Brook!

350
00:27:51.090 --> 00:27:52.100
Sir Bones!

351
00:27:53.240 --> 00:27:55.640
I finally managed to protect you!

352
00:27:59.200 --> 00:28:00.980
Please allow me to handle the rest!

353
00:28:01.780 --> 00:28:04.210
Tsk! How arrogant!

354
00:28:04.210 --> 00:28:06.820
Sheep's Horn!

355
00:28:09.800 --> 00:28:11.230
What?!

356
00:28:11.230 --> 00:28:12.660
What are those arms?

357
00:28:12.660 --> 00:28:13.840
Sir Bones!

358
00:28:14.620 --> 00:28:16.080
Take this!

359
00:28:16.080 --> 00:28:18.320
Soul Parade!

360
00:28:23.780 --> 00:28:25.440
Sir Bones, that is amazing!

361
00:28:28.040 --> 00:28:30.400
What manner of ability is this?

362
00:28:34.180 --> 00:28:35.480
Brook!

363
00:28:35.480 --> 00:28:37.120
Keep stalling him!

364
00:28:38.920 --> 00:28:41.080
Diable Mouton...

365
00:28:41.940 --> 00:28:43.540
Shot!

366
00:28:55.980 --> 00:28:57.460
Sheepshead-sama!

367
00:28:59.480 --> 00:29:00.410
Sanji-kun!

368
00:29:00.410 --> 00:29:03.380
Oh, Nami-swan!

369
00:29:04.580 --> 00:29:06.180
Who are you people?!

370
00:29:06.180 --> 00:29:08.100
And just who are you people...

371
00:29:10.160 --> 00:29:11.620
What? How creepy!

372
00:29:12.640 --> 00:29:14.180
Ginrummy-sama!

373
00:29:15.140 --> 00:29:17.770
You lot there! Retreat!

374
00:29:17.770 --> 00:29:19.770
Sheepshead-sama has been done in!

375
00:29:19.770 --> 00:29:20.940
What?!

376
00:29:20.940 --> 00:29:23.130
But we haven't found the samurai yet!

377
00:29:23.130 --> 00:29:26.270
We've cornered them this far,
and he still hasn't shown himself!

378
00:29:26.270 --> 00:29:29.140
"The samurai's not here." Tell him exactly that!

379
00:29:29.140 --> 00:29:29.820
Yes, ma'am!

380
00:29:35.180 --> 00:29:36.660
The water's draining away...

381
00:29:39.220 --> 00:29:40.620
What was that all about, I wonder?

382
00:29:41.260 --> 00:29:43.870
It's certainly one strange island.

383
00:29:43.870 --> 00:29:46.150
I hope that girl's okay, too...

384
00:29:46.150 --> 00:29:49.630
She's more agile than we are. She'll be quite alright.

385
00:29:49.630 --> 00:29:50.570
You're right.

386
00:29:58.920 --> 00:30:01.080
Hey, guys!

387
00:30:02.040 --> 00:30:04.060
Get over here right now!

388
00:30:04.820 --> 00:30:08.080
That be Chop'emon, in the lower forest!

389
00:30:08.080 --> 00:30:10.140
Then let's move out! There's no time to lose!

390
00:30:18.240 --> 00:30:20.890
<b>The Kid Pirates' Safe House</b>

391
00:30:31.440 --> 00:30:32.660
What's that noise?

392
00:30:37.660 --> 00:30:39.020
What happened?

393
00:30:39.020 --> 00:30:42.250
Captain, there's a massive hole!

394
00:30:42.250 --> 00:30:43.470
A hole?

395
00:30:43.470 --> 00:30:44.740
Something's landed!

396
00:30:46.220 --> 00:30:47.590
Take arms!

397
00:30:47.590 --> 00:30:49.770
Yeah!

398
00:30:51.120 --> 00:30:52.130
That's it!

399
00:31:08.610 --> 00:31:10.780
It certainly is quite large.

400
00:31:11.440 --> 00:31:13.250
Where did it fall from?

401
00:31:13.250 --> 00:31:15.720
Just who in the hell caused this?!

402
00:31:17.180 --> 00:31:19.760
Hey, doesn't it look human-shaped?

403
00:31:20.980 --> 00:31:22.160
If I recall correctly...

404
00:31:22.760 --> 00:31:27.640
There's a legend about a sky island where some monster lives...

405
00:31:28.860 --> 00:31:31.360
Somewhere in the sky, around here, right?

406
00:31:32.500 --> 00:31:35.960
Are you telling me that it was pushed off of a sky island?!

407
00:31:37.540 --> 00:31:38.640
Captain Kid!

408
00:31:39.420 --> 00:31:42.450
One of our ships was capsized by the impact!

409
00:31:42.450 --> 00:31:43.620
What'd you say?!

410
00:31:44.960 --> 00:31:47.860
Damn it all! Who did this?!

411
00:31:48.680 --> 00:31:52.500
The strong live, and the weak die.

412
00:31:53.460 --> 00:31:56.640
That is just how the world is.

413
00:31:58.700 --> 00:32:00.880
A few minutes ago...

414
00:32:03.300 --> 00:32:07.800
<b>Sky Island - The Ruins of Balloon Terminal</b>

415
00:32:14.900 --> 00:32:17.060
What exactly are you doing?

416
00:32:17.060 --> 00:32:19.290
Let us leave him be, High Priest!

417
00:32:19.290 --> 00:32:20.980
He must be insane!

418
00:32:20.980 --> 00:32:24.720
We're ten thousand meters up in the air.

419
00:32:24.720 --> 00:32:29.120
This man was looking for a place to die.

420
00:32:29.120 --> 00:32:31.160
If he's serious, why bother to stop him?

421
00:32:33.220 --> 00:32:35.580
To sum up his life,

422
00:32:35.580 --> 00:32:39.180
he had been defeated seven times as a pirate,

423
00:32:40.720 --> 00:32:44.620
and was captured by the Navy or his enemies eighteen times.

424
00:32:45.900 --> 00:32:51.820
He underwent torture repeatedly, and lived as a criminal.

425
00:33:00.860 --> 00:33:03.910
He wanted to commit suicide...

426
00:33:05.020 --> 00:33:09.160
in an extraordinary way by jumping off of a sky island.

427
00:33:13.500 --> 00:33:16.370
Hence, the current situation.

428
00:33:19.130 --> 00:33:20.960
It bears repeating:

429
00:33:20.960 --> 00:33:24.100
Single-handedly, he challenged
the Navy and the Emperors,

430
00:33:24.100 --> 00:33:28.590
was captured eighteen times,
and sentenced to death forty times.

431
00:33:29.260 --> 00:33:33.280
When hanged, the chain broke.

432
00:33:33.940 --> 00:33:37.980
When put under the guillotine,
the blade shattered.

433
00:33:39.500 --> 00:33:42.250
When sentenced to impalement,
the spear splintered.

434
00:33:43.190 --> 00:33:47.560
Consequently, he sank nine prison ships.

435
00:33:47.560 --> 00:33:51.260
In short, no one could kill him.

436
00:33:52.280 --> 00:33:55.830
And that included himself.

437
00:34:02.420 --> 00:34:03.820
What is it now?

438
00:34:19.780 --> 00:34:22.140
What the hell is that monster?

439
00:34:22.770 --> 00:34:26.250
Damn, my head hurts.

440
00:34:27.380 --> 00:34:30.280
Guess it's hard to die.

441
00:34:30.280 --> 00:34:32.540
I survived again.

442
00:34:36.700 --> 00:34:39.370
I'm impressed he pulled it off...

443
00:34:39.370 --> 00:34:41.500
That old man, Whitebeard.

444
00:34:55.520 --> 00:34:58.310
The man searching for his deathbed:

445
00:34:59.300 --> 00:35:01.480
Kaidou of the Beasts

446
00:35:07.620 --> 00:35:13.400
People say, "If it's one-on-one, Kaidou will win."

447
00:35:14.540 --> 00:35:24.290
Whether on land, sea, or air, he is the pirate known as "the mightiest being alive".

448
00:35:28.520 --> 00:35:31.710
I've no choice, have I?!

449
00:35:44.200 --> 00:35:46.100
Damn it all!

450
00:35:47.700 --> 00:35:49.910
Hurry up, Joker!

451
00:35:49.910 --> 00:35:54.860
Make ready for the final battle!

452
00:35:57.100 --> 00:36:00.240
I don't care if this boring world is laid to waste!

453
00:36:01.480 --> 00:36:06.360
Let's start the greatest war the world's ever seen!
